rowth >= 1.7) = 0.715 from my CQ3 — the ~1.5pp wedge is the low-growth/moderate-inflation leftover cell (growth < 1.7 with core 2.0-2.69) that rule 4 assigns to B, net of the growth-2.0-to-2.59 mass also in B. Consistent. (v) I do not accept C's \"grid supply wall\" leg: Panelist 3's arithmetic on AI-Q3 (365 -> 998 TWh is ~72 GW average load, ~$35-75B/yr against OECD-38+China power capex of ~$600-800B/yr) is correct and the binding constraint is interconnection QUEUE TIME, not capital. My C = 23 rests on the inflation-measurement floor plus the late-building care Baumol channel.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:51.519Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"NBS reports a calendar-year real GDP growth rate below 3.5% for any year, absent a declared pandemic or war shock, as reprinted in the IMF WEO.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2029\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the reported-series institutional floor, my single largest CQ3 driver. CQ3 P50 falls from 2.1% to ~1.8% and P90 to ~2.8%; CQ6-A falls from 22 to ~13 and D rises from 7 to ~12; CQ4 P50 falls ~15bp on the lower-g channel. This is the cleanest single falsifier of my whole payload.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"US BLS data (OES median hourly by industry, or ECI by occupation group) show healthcare-support plus construction-and-extraction real median hourly wages cumulatively BELOW information plus finance plus professional-and-business-services, measured from 2025, for two consecutive annual vintages.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my claim that the required F+Q vs J+K+M divergence is a continuation of an already-running trend rather than a sign flip. CQ1 falls from 23 to ~10, and plank (a) stays at 5 while my attack on Wave 1's dilution contradiction loses its empirical leg.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Türkiye core CPI 12-month av